# HoMM3 assets (copyrighted — supplied locally by the user, never committed)
/public/h3/*
!/public/h3/.gitkeep

# AI-generated raster sprite pack. The baked, right-sized images now live IN the
# repo — the game (and your VPS) serve them straight from public/sprites/ →
# dist/sprites/, so no CDN is needed at runtime. Commit the images together with
# the manifest (index.cdn.json, repointed to ./sprites/<file> by
# scripts/fetch-cdn.mjs). Still ignored: the 512² masters/, and the lab bridge's
# two transient directories, _candidates/ (holding) and _archive/ (promote
# history) — none of which is a resolvable asset. The lab/ my-layer and the
# resolver manifests index.json / overrides.json USED to be ignored too and are
# now committed on purpose: overrides.json maps ids onto ./sprites/lab/<id>.png
# and is the top layer of the resolver in src/gfx/sprites.js, so the art it
# points at has to be in the repo for anyone else to see it.

/public/sprites/_archive
/public/sprites/_candidates
/public/sprites/masters

!/public/sprites/.gitkeep
!/public/sprites/README.md
!/public/sprites/index.cdn.json
!/public/sprites/*.png
!/public/sprites/*.jpg
# The packed atlas pages (public/sprites/atlas/) are NOT committed. They used to
# be, so that a fresh `npm run dev` needed no build step — but they are generated
# output, `npm run build` regenerates them, and 15 MB of unmergeable WebP churned
# in the working tree on every build. That is what produced the one revert
# (747a0aa), and the committed copy had already drifted 31 sprites behind the PNGs
# without anyone noticing — generated output masquerading as source, silently
# wrong. They are now rebuilt on demand: `npm run build` always repacks, and
# `npm run dev` repacks via `predev` only when the PNGs are newer (~20s once after
# a clone, ~0s thereafter). The per-file PNGs above remain the source of truth,
# and the runtime falls back to loading them individually if no atlas exists.
#
# THIS RULE HAD TO BE WRITTEN OUT AGAIN. It used to be carried implicitly by a
# blanket `/public/sprites/*` above; when that was replaced with the three
# targeted ignores, the atlas lost its only protection and 15 MB of pages were
# committed — leaving this paragraph standing over nothing, describing a policy
# that no longer had a rule behind it. It came straight back too: a plain
# `npm run build` repacked the same 702 sprites into the same 11 pages and
# produced a ~6 MB binary diff, because the packer's shelf layout is not
# byte-stable. An explicit path is harder to lose than an implicit one.
/public/sprites/atlas/

# Editor and tooling backups. `index.cdn.json.bak` and `overrides.json.bak` were
# committed once; nothing resolves them and a backup copy of a manifest is not
# something a built bundle should carry.
*.bak

# AI-generated sound pack. Like sprites, the audio now lives IN the repo (served
# from public/sounds/ → dist/sounds/), so no CDN is needed at runtime. Commit the
# audio together with the manifest (index.cdn.json, repointed to ./sounds/<file>
# by scripts/fetch-cdn.mjs --domain sounds). The local index.json / overrides.json
# resolver layers stay ignored.
/public/sounds/*
!/public/sounds/.gitkeep
!/public/sounds/index.cdn.json
!/public/sounds/*.mp3
!/public/sounds/*.ogg
!/public/sounds/*.wav

# HoMM3 data (copyrighted — supplied locally by the user, never committed)
